#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:41
msgid "How Do Sessions Work?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:43
msgid ""
"When a page is loaded, the session class will check to see if a valid "
"session cookie is sent by the user's browser. If a session cookie does "
"**not** exist (or if it doesn't match one stored on the server or has "
"expired) a new session will be created and saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:48
msgid ""
"If a valid session does exist, its information will be updated. With each"
" update, the session ID may be regenerated if configured to do so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:51
msgid ""
"It's important for you to understand that once initialized, the Session "
"class runs automatically. There is nothing you need to do to cause the "
"above behavior to happen. You can, as you'll see below, work with session"
" data, but the process of reading, writing, and updating a session is "
"automatic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:57
msgid ""
"Under CLI, the Session library will automatically halt itself, as this is"
" a concept based entirely on the HTTP protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:61
msgid "A Note about Concurrency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:63
msgid ""
"Unless you're developing a website with heavy AJAX usage, you can skip "
"this section. If you are, however, and if you're experiencing performance"
" issues, then this note is exactly what you're looking for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:67
msgid ""
"Sessions in CodeIgniter v2.x didn't implement locking, which meant that "
"two HTTP requests using the same session could run exactly at the same "
"time. To use a more appropriate technical term - requests were non-"
"blocking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:72
msgid ""
"However, non-blocking requests in the context of sessions also means "
"unsafe, because, modifications to session data (or session ID "
"regeneration) in one request can interfere with the execution of a "
"second, concurrent request. This detail was at the root of many issues "
"and the main reason why CodeIgniter 3 has a completely re-written Session"
" library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:78
msgid ""
"Why are we telling you this? Because it is likely that after trying to "
"find the reason for your performance issues, you may conclude that "
"locking is the issue and therefore look into how to remove the locks ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:82
msgid ""
"DO NOT DO THAT! Removing locks would be **wrong** and it will cause you "
"more problems!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/sessions.rst:85
msgid ""
"Locking is not the issue, it is a solution. Your issue is that you still "
"have the session open, while you've already processed it and therefore no"
" longer need it. So, what you need is to close the session for the "
"current request after you no longer need it."
msgstr ""

